WEBVTT

00:30.000 --> 00:35.000
Doctor, doctor, help me, I'm choking.

00:35.000 --> 00:36.000
I'm strangulating.

00:36.000 --> 00:39.000
Give me some oxygen, oxygen, never mind the expense.

00:39.000 --> 00:41.000
Now, now, Rowley, it's not as bad as all that.

00:41.000 --> 00:42.000
Take it easy.

00:42.000 --> 00:44.000
Now go ahead and take a deep breath.

00:44.000 --> 00:46.000
There, you see, you can breathe all right.

00:46.000 --> 00:49.000
I don't know, I didn't feel any air go down into my lungs.

00:49.000 --> 00:50.000
I got a hole in my neck.

00:50.000 --> 00:51.000
Yeah, you're right.

00:51.000 --> 00:53.000
Now relax and tell me what happened.

00:53.000 --> 00:55.000
I swallowed a fish and it stabbed me.

00:55.000 --> 00:56.000
Is that all?

00:56.000 --> 00:57.000
A little fish bone.

00:57.000 --> 00:58.000
A little fish bone.

00:58.000 --> 01:01.000
I got a hole thin in my throat with part of the runner.

01:01.000 --> 01:03.000
I tell you, I can't get any air through my gills.

01:03.000 --> 01:04.000
Give me some oxygen.

01:04.000 --> 01:05.000
Now wait a minute.

01:05.000 --> 01:06.000
Open your mouth, you want me to help you?

01:06.000 --> 01:07.000
Let me see.

01:07.000 --> 01:08.000
Say ah.

01:08.000 --> 01:09.000
Ah.

01:09.000 --> 01:10.000
Oh.

01:10.000 --> 01:11.000
What's the matter?

01:11.000 --> 01:12.000
Now he's trying to go upstream.

01:12.000 --> 01:13.000
I can't.

01:13.000 --> 01:16.000
That bone must be a yard long.

01:16.000 --> 01:18.000
It hurts me worse when I'm sitting.

01:18.000 --> 01:19.000
Now, Rowley, relax.

01:19.000 --> 01:21.000
There's no bone lodged in your throat.

01:21.000 --> 01:22.000
Although it did leave a slight scratch,

01:22.000 --> 01:24.000
but it'll be all right in a few hours.

01:24.000 --> 01:25.000
A slight scratch?

01:25.000 --> 01:26.000
Yes.

01:26.000 --> 01:27.000
Oh.

01:27.000 --> 01:28.000
Is that all?

01:28.000 --> 01:29.000
Yes.

01:29.000 --> 01:32.000
Well, I guess I'll go back and finish the fish.

01:32.000 --> 01:34.000
They don't give you any rebate at that lunchroom

01:34.000 --> 01:36.000
for what you leave on your plate.

01:36.000 --> 01:37.000
What do I owe you, sir?

01:37.000 --> 01:38.000
Nothing.

01:38.000 --> 01:40.000
This is on the Stephenson Aircraft Company.

01:40.000 --> 01:42.000
Gee, that's a good deal.

01:42.000 --> 01:44.000
I got to get sick more often if it's on the cuff.

01:44.000 --> 01:45.000
Well, thanks a lot, Doc.

01:45.000 --> 01:46.000
Just a minute, Rowley.

01:46.000 --> 01:48.000
You seem to have a condition much more serious

01:48.000 --> 01:50.000
than a fish bone.

01:50.000 --> 01:51.000
I have?

01:51.000 --> 01:52.000
Yeah.

01:52.000 --> 01:53.000
Open your mouth again.

01:53.000 --> 01:54.000
A chicken bone?

01:54.000 --> 01:55.000
No.

01:55.000 --> 01:56.000
Open your mouth again.

01:56.000 --> 01:57.000
Wider.

01:57.000 --> 01:59.000
Mm.

01:59.000 --> 02:02.000
Mm-hmm.

02:02.000 --> 02:03.000
Is it that serious?

02:03.000 --> 02:05.000
Well, not too serious.

02:05.000 --> 02:07.000
That is, if you have them out right away.

02:07.000 --> 02:09.000
Have them out?

02:09.000 --> 02:11.000
How can you see my appendix from way up here?

02:11.000 --> 02:13.000
Not your appendix, Rowley.

02:13.000 --> 02:14.000
Your tonsils.

02:14.000 --> 02:15.000
Oh, my tonsils.

02:15.000 --> 02:16.000
Certainly.

02:16.000 --> 02:19.000
Well, I don't think I'll bother about having them taken out.

02:19.000 --> 02:20.000
I've had my tonsils since I was a kid.

02:20.000 --> 02:22.000
They're sort of attached to them.

02:22.000 --> 02:23.000
Now, just a minute, Rowley.

02:23.000 --> 02:25.000
If you don't have those tonsils out right away,

02:25.000 --> 02:27.000
something serious may develop.

02:27.000 --> 02:29.000
Serious?

02:29.000 --> 02:31.000
Beyond the level?

02:31.000 --> 02:33.000
Otitis media?

02:33.000 --> 02:34.000
Septicemia?

02:34.000 --> 02:35.000
Rheumatic?

02:35.000 --> 02:36.000
Endocarditis?

02:36.000 --> 02:37.000
Quincy?

02:37.000 --> 02:38.000
Quincy.

02:38.000 --> 02:39.000
Yes.

02:39.000 --> 02:41.000
So you see, an operation is really necessary.

02:41.000 --> 02:42.000
An operation?

02:42.000 --> 02:43.000
Yeah.

02:43.000 --> 02:44.000
But, Doc, couldn't I cure it myself?

02:44.000 --> 02:46.000
Oh, certainly not.

02:46.000 --> 02:48.000
Maybe if I read that book, the Quincy Report.

02:48.000 --> 02:50.000
Now, look, Rowley.

02:50.000 --> 02:53.000
In your case, an operation is specifically indicated.

02:53.000 --> 02:55.000
Put an operation?

02:55.000 --> 02:57.000
Maybe I could wait until they got ripe and dropped off.

02:57.000 --> 02:59.000
Oh, stop acting like an infant.

02:59.000 --> 03:02.000
Why, a tonsillectomy is as simple as ABC.

03:02.000 --> 03:04.000
There's nothing to it.

03:04.000 --> 03:08.000
We just take a small instrument about, oh, no larger than this.

03:08.000 --> 03:09.000
You see?

03:09.000 --> 03:10.000
Snip, snip, and they're out.

03:10.000 --> 03:12.000
I'll make a reservation for you at the hospital.

03:12.000 --> 03:13.000
Okay, let's say next year.

03:13.000 --> 03:15.000
No, tomorrow.

03:15.000 --> 03:18.000
Riley, those tonsils must come out.

03:18.000 --> 03:20.000
Hello, dear.

03:20.000 --> 03:21.000
Hello, Dumpling.

03:21.000 --> 03:22.000
You're up late tonight.

03:22.000 --> 03:23.000
Hello, Pop.

03:23.000 --> 03:24.000
Hello, Daddy.

03:24.000 --> 03:25.000
Hello, children.

03:25.000 --> 03:26.000
I hope you're hungry.

03:26.000 --> 03:27.000
I just fixed the most delicious.

03:27.000 --> 03:28.000
Riley, what's the matter?

03:28.000 --> 03:30.000
I can tell by your face something's wrong.

03:30.000 --> 03:31.000
Nothing's wrong.

03:31.000 --> 03:32.000
Everything's great.

03:32.000 --> 03:33.000
Daddy, what is it?

03:33.000 --> 03:34.000
Tell me, dear.

03:34.000 --> 03:35.000
It's really nothing.

03:35.000 --> 03:37.000
I'd rather not even talk about it.

03:37.000 --> 03:39.000
I'd rather suffer.

03:39.000 --> 03:40.000
Suffer in silence.

03:40.000 --> 03:42.000
Oh, Riley, tell me, what is it?

03:42.000 --> 03:44.000
Peg, I'm a sick man.

03:44.000 --> 03:45.000
Oh, no, darling.

03:45.000 --> 03:47.000
Daddy, oh, Daddy.

03:47.000 --> 03:49.000
Gee, Pop, you better sit down.

03:49.000 --> 03:51.000
Peg, help me over to the chair.

03:51.000 --> 03:55.000
Oh, my sweet darling, of course I will.

03:55.000 --> 03:57.000
Here's a pillow, Pop.

03:57.000 --> 03:58.000
Thanks, Junior.

03:58.000 --> 04:00.000
Daddy, shall I put on your slippers?

04:00.000 --> 04:03.000
OK, but I think you'll find them a little too large for you.

04:03.000 --> 04:04.000
Oh, sweetheart, what happened?

04:04.000 --> 04:05.000
I can't stand it.

04:05.000 --> 04:07.000
I saw the doctor today where I work.

04:07.000 --> 04:08.000
The doctor?

04:08.000 --> 04:10.000
About what?

04:10.000 --> 04:12.000
Peg, you've got to be brave.

04:12.000 --> 04:14.000
Prepare yourself for a shock.

04:14.000 --> 04:15.000
Oh, sweetheart, what is it?

04:15.000 --> 04:17.000
A lot of things.

04:17.000 --> 04:22.000
Carditis, end of the carditis, and September Santa Anita.

04:22.000 --> 04:24.000
Oh, really?

04:24.000 --> 04:28.000
That's what I'll get if I don't have my tonsils taken out.

04:28.000 --> 04:29.000
Tonsils?

04:29.000 --> 04:32.000
Oh, yes, yes, please.

04:32.000 --> 04:35.000
Gosh, Pop, I thought you were going to keep the pocket.

04:35.000 --> 04:37.000
Don't be so disappointed.

04:37.000 --> 04:40.000
I tell you, I'm a sick man, a very sick man.

04:40.000 --> 04:45.000
My life is hanging by a thread, one tug and I, but I can take it.

04:45.000 --> 04:48.000
I've got a good, clean life, and if I have to go, well...

04:48.000 --> 04:50.000
Oh, don't be!

04:50.000 --> 04:52.000
I'm certainly glad everybody's glad.

04:52.000 --> 04:54.000
I'm glad my tonsils tickle you.

04:54.000 --> 04:58.000
I'm sorry, dear, but there's nothing to a tonsil operation.

04:58.000 --> 05:00.000
Nothing to it, she says.

05:00.000 --> 05:03.000
They're going to slip my throat from ear to ear and rip out my tonsils,

05:03.000 --> 05:05.000
and she says there's nothing to it.

05:05.000 --> 05:07.000
Well, Pop, they may not even cut your tonsils out.

05:07.000 --> 05:09.000
They may burn them out like a kid at school.

05:09.000 --> 05:10.000
Burn them out?

05:10.000 --> 05:11.000
There's nothing to it.

05:11.000 --> 05:13.000
Nobody's shoving a blowtorch down my throat.

05:13.000 --> 05:15.000
It's a minor operation. You won't even feel it.

05:15.000 --> 05:18.000
You can say that again, because I ain't even going to the hospital.

05:18.000 --> 05:21.000
Oh, Patty, it's an absolutely minor operation.

05:21.000 --> 05:22.000
Of course, be sensible.

05:22.000 --> 05:24.000
If your tonsils have to go, they have to go.

05:24.000 --> 05:26.000
Yeah, but I don't want to go with them.

05:26.000 --> 05:29.000
You're just exaggerating things in your mind.

05:29.000 --> 05:31.000
Gee, Pop, I never thought you'd be a coward.

05:31.000 --> 05:33.000
A coward?

05:33.000 --> 05:35.000
I am not a coward.

05:35.000 --> 05:37.000
I'm just scared.

05:37.000 --> 05:40.000
I mean, a few kids and your mother.

05:40.000 --> 05:44.000
Here you are all alone, and tomorrow, tomorrow,

05:44.000 --> 05:46.000
tomorrow I go to the hospital.

05:46.000 --> 05:48.000
Well, cheer up, Pop.

05:48.000 --> 05:49.000
We'll get along without you.

05:49.000 --> 05:50.000
Why?

05:50.000 --> 05:52.000
I mean, till you come home.

05:52.000 --> 05:53.000
Don't worry about us, dear.

05:53.000 --> 05:54.000
We'll be all right.

05:54.000 --> 05:58.000
Well, that makes me feel a little better.

05:58.000 --> 06:01.000
Gee, you ought to know by now that I'm no coward.

06:01.000 --> 06:03.000
I'm not afraid of anything or anybody.

06:03.000 --> 06:05.000
Don't you remember that time at Ebbets Field

06:05.000 --> 06:08.000
when that six-foot umpire got the licking of his life?

06:08.000 --> 06:10.000
I was one of the 12 guys that gave it to him.

06:10.000 --> 06:12.000
Sure, Pop, I'm sorry.

06:12.000 --> 06:14.000
You're no coward.

06:14.000 --> 06:17.000
After all, what's a tonsil operation, anyway?

06:17.000 --> 06:19.000
The doctor explained exactly how they do it.

06:19.000 --> 06:21.000
Of course, they do them every day, dozens of them.

06:21.000 --> 06:22.000
There's nothing to it.

06:22.000 --> 06:23.000
It's a cinch.

06:23.000 --> 06:24.000
All they do is they take a knife.

06:24.000 --> 06:27.000
It's about as big as, well, it's about from,

06:27.000 --> 06:29.000
it's about,

06:29.000 --> 06:33.000
about from here to where Junior's standing.

06:33.000 --> 06:35.000
And they shove it down my throat.

06:35.000 --> 06:37.000
And they chop.

06:37.000 --> 06:42.000
And they, oh, oh, oh, oh.

06:42.000 --> 06:48.000
You say this, Frank, and someone comes, finally.

06:48.000 --> 06:50.000
Oh, yes, Dr. Harvey.

06:50.000 --> 06:52.000
Hang up, partner.

06:52.000 --> 06:53.000
Yes, doctor.

06:53.000 --> 06:55.000
Oh, he's fine.

06:55.000 --> 06:56.000
When?

06:56.000 --> 06:57.000
He'll be there.

06:57.000 --> 06:58.000
Thank you, doctor.

06:58.000 --> 06:59.000
Goodbye.

06:59.000 --> 07:00.000
That was Dr. Harvey,

07:00.000 --> 07:03.000
phone to say he'll operate at 9 in the morning.

07:03.000 --> 07:05.000
I'm having that phone taken out.

07:05.000 --> 07:07.000
Now, don't start fooling me again.

07:07.000 --> 07:09.000
The whole thing will be over before you know it.

07:09.000 --> 07:10.000
That's what I'm afraid of.

07:10.000 --> 07:12.000
When it's over, will I know it?

07:12.000 --> 07:13.000
Maybe I ought to see another Dr. Peyton,

07:13.000 --> 07:15.000
one of those herb doctors.

07:15.000 --> 07:17.000
Look, Riley, you can't remove tonsils with herbs.

07:17.000 --> 07:19.000
And the doctors go to your tonsils,

07:19.000 --> 07:20.000
they've got to come out.

07:20.000 --> 07:23.000
Sure, it's okay for him to say my tonsils have got to come out.

07:23.000 --> 07:24.000
I'm wise to them, doctors.

07:24.000 --> 07:26.000
Fake thing tonsils grow on trees.

07:26.000 --> 07:28.000
Well, why should he insist on an operation

07:28.000 --> 07:29.000
if it weren't necessary?

07:29.000 --> 07:30.000
You're not paying him.

07:30.000 --> 07:32.000
He gets the same salary from the plant

07:32.000 --> 07:33.000
whether he operates or not.

07:33.000 --> 07:34.000
That don't fool me.

07:34.000 --> 07:35.000
I know doctors.

07:35.000 --> 07:36.000
They love to operate.

07:36.000 --> 07:37.000
It's a disease with them.

07:37.000 --> 07:39.000
Oh, Daddy, it's nothing.

07:39.000 --> 07:42.000
I had my tonsils taken out when I was only six.

07:42.000 --> 07:44.000
You were too young to know what you were doing.

07:44.000 --> 07:47.000
Listen, dear, you need to get your mind off of it for a while.

07:47.000 --> 07:49.000
Why don't you go over and dab a while with Jim Dillon?

07:57.000 --> 07:58.000
Why don't he answer?

07:58.000 --> 08:01.000
Why don't he answer?

08:02.000 --> 08:05.000
It's funny, his lights are on.

08:05.000 --> 08:07.000
Hey, Gillis!

08:07.000 --> 08:09.000
Oh, Gillis!

08:09.000 --> 08:10.000
Gillis!

08:10.000 --> 08:11.000
Yeah, Riley.

08:11.000 --> 08:12.000
Answer the phone.

08:12.000 --> 08:13.000
I want to talk to you.

08:13.000 --> 08:14.000
Go ahead, talk.

08:14.000 --> 08:16.000
Listen, Gillis.

08:16.000 --> 08:19.000
What are you doing over here when you're supposed to be over there?

08:19.000 --> 08:21.000
Your lights was on, so I tried the door, so here I am.

08:21.000 --> 08:22.000
Hiya, pal.

08:22.000 --> 08:24.000
How's about a little game of gin rummy?

08:24.000 --> 08:26.000
Usual type steaks.

08:26.000 --> 08:27.000
I don't know.

08:27.000 --> 08:28.000
I'm too lucky.

08:28.000 --> 08:29.000
Luck nothing.

08:29.000 --> 08:30.000
Science.

08:30.000 --> 08:31.000
Ten cents a game?

08:31.000 --> 08:33.000
Okay, go ahead and deal.

08:33.000 --> 08:34.000
I already dealt.

08:34.000 --> 08:36.000
Those ain't fingernails you got in your hands.

08:36.000 --> 08:38.000
They're cards.

08:38.000 --> 08:39.000
I go first.

08:39.000 --> 08:40.000
Hey!

08:40.000 --> 08:42.000
What happened to you down at the plant today?

08:42.000 --> 08:45.000
You went off for four for lunch and never came back.

08:45.000 --> 08:46.000
Well, you see, it was like this.

08:46.000 --> 08:49.000
I had some trouble.

08:49.000 --> 08:50.000
My turn.

08:50.000 --> 08:51.000
I was worried about you.

08:51.000 --> 08:56.000
I didn't realize you was missing until suddenly the belt line started going faster.

08:56.000 --> 08:58.000
I had some terrible trouble.

08:58.000 --> 09:00.000
My turn.

09:00.000 --> 09:02.000
If Riley, my pal, is in trouble, then I couldn't stand.

09:02.000 --> 09:03.000
I know.

09:03.000 --> 09:05.000
You got fired.

09:05.000 --> 09:07.000
It was worse trouble than that.

09:07.000 --> 09:09.000
I got to go to the hospital tomorrow.

09:09.000 --> 09:11.000
My turn.

09:11.000 --> 09:12.000
Hospital?

09:12.000 --> 09:13.000
What?

09:13.000 --> 09:14.000
Hey!

09:14.000 --> 09:15.000
What's the trouble?

09:15.000 --> 09:16.000
There's nothing wrong with you, is there, pal?

09:16.000 --> 09:18.000
Oh, if there's anything wrong with you, you're my best friend.

09:18.000 --> 09:19.000
It's my tonsils.

09:19.000 --> 09:20.000
Tonsils?

09:20.000 --> 09:21.000
Is that all?

09:21.000 --> 09:23.000
Ain't that enough?

09:23.000 --> 09:25.000
My turn.

09:25.000 --> 09:27.000
You got a nerve aggravating me over a couple of measly tonsils.

09:27.000 --> 09:29.000
Ain't you got no consideration?

09:29.000 --> 09:30.000
It's easy for you to say.

09:30.000 --> 09:32.000
What do you know about it, Gillis?

09:32.000 --> 09:33.000
I know plenty about surgery.

09:33.000 --> 09:38.000
Why, at the end of the day, it goes by I don't read all the obituary columns.

09:38.000 --> 09:39.000
My turn.

09:39.000 --> 09:40.000
Sorry.

09:40.000 --> 09:42.000
Taking out tonsils is a cinch.

09:42.000 --> 09:43.000
There's nothing to it.

09:43.000 --> 09:46.000
Any good doctor can perform that operation blindfolded.

09:46.000 --> 09:47.000
Blindfolded, huh?

09:47.000 --> 09:51.000
Well, my doctor, if he wants to get paid, better take a peek.

09:51.000 --> 09:53.000
My turn.

09:53.000 --> 09:56.000
My hand don't seem to be getting any better.

09:56.000 --> 09:58.000
You're in bad shape, rather.

09:58.000 --> 09:59.000
Scared stiff.

09:59.000 --> 10:00.000
Now, why don't you relax?

10:00.000 --> 10:01.000
There's nothing to it.

10:01.000 --> 10:03.000
Oh, what do you know about it?

10:03.000 --> 10:05.000
Have you ever had your tonsils taken out?

10:05.000 --> 10:08.000
No, but believe me, I'd be glad to if I ever had the opportunity.

10:08.000 --> 10:11.000
Boy, would I love to go to a hospital and stay overnight.

10:11.000 --> 10:13.000
24 wonderful hours away from my wife.

10:13.000 --> 10:15.000
Some wife.

10:15.000 --> 10:17.000
Ether is better.

10:17.000 --> 10:18.000
That's it.

10:18.000 --> 10:21.000
Gin.

10:21.000 --> 10:23.000
Well, I like my wife.

10:23.000 --> 10:24.000
She's cute.

10:24.000 --> 10:25.000
And I like my tonsils.

10:25.000 --> 10:26.000
They're cute, too.

10:26.000 --> 10:27.000
Silence.

10:27.000 --> 10:28.000
Turn your face this way.

10:28.000 --> 10:29.000
A little more.

10:29.000 --> 10:30.000
I want to tell you something to your face.

10:30.000 --> 10:31.000
You're a coward.

10:31.000 --> 10:33.000
I am not a coward.

10:33.000 --> 10:34.000
Then stop squawking.

10:34.000 --> 10:36.000
If the doctor says you've got to do it, you've got to do it.

10:36.000 --> 10:38.000
The whole thing will only take a minute.

10:38.000 --> 10:39.000
Only a minute, huh?

10:39.000 --> 10:40.000
Sure.

10:40.000 --> 10:43.000
They put you to sleep, and they open your mouth.

10:43.000 --> 10:46.000
They take a very sharp instrument.

10:46.000 --> 10:48.000
Down your throat it goes.

10:48.000 --> 10:50.000
Very delicate.

10:50.000 --> 10:51.000
Slash, slash, rip, rip, rip.

10:51.000 --> 10:52.000
It goes.

10:52.000 --> 10:53.000
Yeah.

10:53.000 --> 10:54.000
I knew it.

10:54.000 --> 10:55.000
You're a coward.

10:55.000 --> 10:56.000
No, I did not, Gilligan.

10:56.000 --> 10:58.000
Now, let me relieve your mind, pal.

10:58.000 --> 11:00.000
You know that Mrs. Bennett on the next block?

11:00.000 --> 11:02.000
My wife sees her in the market.

11:02.000 --> 11:04.000
Well, she had her tonsils taken out, and the very next day,

11:04.000 --> 11:05.000
she was giving a party.

11:05.000 --> 11:06.000
My wife told me.

11:06.000 --> 11:07.000
The next day.

11:07.000 --> 11:08.000
Sure.

11:08.000 --> 11:09.000
You don't have to take my word for it.

11:09.000 --> 11:10.000
Go ask the woman.

11:10.000 --> 11:13.000
And if you need courage, she'll give you plenty of.

11:13.000 --> 11:15.000
I do not need courage.

11:15.000 --> 11:18.000
It'll be a dark and stormy day before Chester A. Riley has

11:18.000 --> 11:20.000
to go to some poor helpless woman for courage.

11:23.000 --> 11:24.000
Somebody's coming.

11:24.000 --> 11:26.000
Now you'll see there's nothing to it.

11:26.000 --> 11:28.000
Not Denise's.

11:28.000 --> 11:29.000
Yes?

11:29.000 --> 11:30.000
Hello.

11:30.000 --> 11:31.000
Is Mrs. Bennett in?

11:31.000 --> 11:32.000
Who should I say is calling?

11:32.000 --> 11:33.000
Riley.

11:33.000 --> 11:35.000
Chester A. Riley.

11:35.000 --> 11:38.000
I live down the street, and we found out that Mrs. Bennett

11:38.000 --> 11:40.000
was just in the hospital.

11:40.000 --> 11:42.000
And the same thing's going to happen to me.

11:42.000 --> 11:43.000
Oh?

11:43.000 --> 11:45.000
So, well, you know, I thought maybe she

11:45.000 --> 11:46.000
could give me some advice.

11:46.000 --> 11:47.000
I'll tell her you're here.

11:47.000 --> 11:48.000
Come in, please.

11:52.000 --> 11:54.000
Who is that at the door, Matilda?

11:54.000 --> 11:56.000
It's a Mr. Riley from down the block, ma'am.

11:56.000 --> 11:58.000
He must have heard about you giving birth to the twins,

11:58.000 --> 12:00.000
and I think he wants a little advice.

12:00.000 --> 12:02.000
I guess his wife is expecting.

12:02.000 --> 12:03.000
I guess so, ma'am.

12:03.000 --> 12:05.000
Well, then you'd better finish feeding the twins.

12:05.000 --> 12:09.000
I know how nervous a prospective father can be.

12:09.000 --> 12:13.000
Oh, Mr. Riley, come on in here.

12:13.000 --> 12:14.000
Hello, Mrs. Bennett.

12:14.000 --> 12:15.000
Hello.

12:15.000 --> 12:16.000
This is my friend, Gillis.

12:16.000 --> 12:17.000
How do you do, ma'am?

12:17.000 --> 12:18.000
How do you do?

12:18.000 --> 12:19.000
Go ahead, Riley.

12:19.000 --> 12:20.000
Get it over with.

12:20.000 --> 12:22.000
Oh, do sit down, gentlemen.

12:22.000 --> 12:24.000
Mr. Riley, I realize what a strain

12:24.000 --> 12:26.000
you must be going through.

12:26.000 --> 12:30.000
Well, I am a little nervous, but mostly on account of my wife.

12:30.000 --> 12:31.000
Well, naturally.

12:31.000 --> 12:35.000
After all, it's your wife's problem, too, isn't it?

12:35.000 --> 12:38.000
Why couldn't this thing have happened when I was single?

12:38.000 --> 12:41.000
Oh, you're retaining your sense of humor.

12:41.000 --> 12:43.000
But now I realize how upset you must be.

12:43.000 --> 12:47.000
But just remember, this sort of thing happens every day.

12:47.000 --> 12:48.000
Now, take my case.

12:48.000 --> 12:49.000
I had two of them.

12:49.000 --> 12:51.000
Two of them?

12:51.000 --> 12:53.000
Doesn't everybody have two?

12:53.000 --> 12:55.000
Oh, Mr. Riley.

12:55.000 --> 13:00.000
But now that it's all over, my husband and I are so happy.

13:00.000 --> 13:04.000
Would you like to see them?

13:04.000 --> 13:06.000
See them?

13:06.000 --> 13:09.000
You mean you brought them home with you?

13:09.000 --> 13:11.000
Oh, and you know something?

13:11.000 --> 13:15.000
I can't tell one from the other.

13:15.000 --> 13:16.000
That don't bother me.

13:16.000 --> 13:19.000
I'm leaving mine at the hospital.

13:19.000 --> 13:20.000
Say that.

13:20.000 --> 13:23.000
Well, you'll love them just like I love mine.

13:23.000 --> 13:26.000
You know, my husband can't wait to get home each night

13:26.000 --> 13:29.000
and play with them.

13:29.000 --> 13:33.000
Play with them?

13:33.000 --> 13:36.000
I don't say.

13:36.000 --> 13:39.000
I think I'd better be going.

13:39.000 --> 13:42.000
If you'll come inside, I'll let you hold one.

13:42.000 --> 13:44.000
With bare hands?

13:44.000 --> 13:46.000
Oh, you'll need both hands, Mr. Riley.

13:46.000 --> 13:48.000
They're quite large, you know.

13:48.000 --> 13:50.000
Large?

13:50.000 --> 13:51.000
How large?

13:51.000 --> 13:55.000
Oh, they each weigh seven pounds.

13:55.000 --> 13:57.000
Seven pounds?

13:57.000 --> 13:59.000
I don't believe it.

13:59.000 --> 14:03.000
And they eat like little piggies.

14:03.000 --> 14:05.000
I shouldn't have come.

14:05.000 --> 14:06.000
They eat?

14:06.000 --> 14:08.000
Mrs. Bennet, what kind of tonsils have you got?

14:08.000 --> 14:11.000
They ought to be involved.

14:11.000 --> 14:13.000
What are you talking about?

14:13.000 --> 14:14.000
My tonsils.

14:14.000 --> 14:15.000
I got to have them out.

14:15.000 --> 14:17.000
Tonsils?

14:17.000 --> 14:19.000
Oh, I see.

14:19.000 --> 14:24.000
Oh, the maid said, and I thought.

14:24.000 --> 14:26.000
I had my tonsils out a year ago.

14:26.000 --> 14:28.000
I was talking about my two baby girls.

14:28.000 --> 14:30.000
I just had twins.

14:30.000 --> 14:31.000
Just had twins?

14:31.000 --> 14:34.000
Yes, twin girls.

14:34.000 --> 14:37.000
Congratulations, ma'am.

14:37.000 --> 14:41.000
Thank you, ma'am.

14:41.000 --> 14:42.000
Oh, there you are.

14:42.000 --> 14:44.000
Come on, it's time to get started for the hospital.

14:44.000 --> 14:46.000
I'm coming, Peg.

14:46.000 --> 14:50.000
But before I do, I've got something to say to my family.

14:50.000 --> 14:51.000
Peg, you sit here.

14:51.000 --> 14:53.000
But you'll be late.

14:53.000 --> 14:55.000
Babs, you sit there.

14:55.000 --> 14:57.000
Junior, you sit there.

14:57.000 --> 14:59.000
Daddy, what's this all about?

14:59.000 --> 15:02.000
I've got something to read to you.

15:02.000 --> 15:04.000
It's in this envelope.

15:04.000 --> 15:10.000
It says, Chester A. Reilly, his last will and testament.

15:10.000 --> 15:12.000
It'll be read after his funeral.

15:12.000 --> 15:14.000
So now I'll read it.

15:14.000 --> 15:15.000
Reilly, will you please stop this?

15:15.000 --> 15:16.000
It's ridiculous.

15:16.000 --> 15:17.000
Sure, Pop.

15:17.000 --> 15:18.000
You're not going to kick off.

15:18.000 --> 15:20.000
Don't be so pessimistic.

15:20.000 --> 15:22.000
Now listen.

15:22.000 --> 15:32.000
It says, it says, I, Chester A. Reilly, of sound body,

15:32.000 --> 15:36.000
hereby cut up my entire estate to wit and ergo.

15:36.000 --> 15:42.000
To Peg, my beloved wife, I leave outright my entire bank

15:42.000 --> 15:46.000
account, which has always been in her name.

15:46.000 --> 15:49.000
Also, for the past year, I have been kind of holding out

15:49.000 --> 15:52.000
a certain sum each week from my salary.

15:52.000 --> 15:53.000
Reilly.

15:53.000 --> 15:54.000
For emergencies.

15:54.000 --> 15:57.000
I want my dear wife to have this $15,

15:57.000 --> 16:00.000
which you will find in the radio behind the third tube

16:00.000 --> 16:02.000
from the left.

16:02.000 --> 16:03.000
Oh, Daddy, please.

16:03.000 --> 16:06.000
Please, Babs, don't interrupt.

16:06.000 --> 16:11.000
To my beloved son and pal, Junior, I leave my good name.

16:11.000 --> 16:13.000
Is that all?

16:13.000 --> 16:15.000
I'm not finished.

16:15.000 --> 16:18.000
Also, I leave him my shoe trees I got for Christmas,

16:18.000 --> 16:21.000
which he will find in my sneakers.

16:21.000 --> 16:24.000
For my darling daughter, Babs, who in the years to come

16:24.000 --> 16:27.000
won't have her father's protecting hand to guide her

16:27.000 --> 16:30.000
when she goes on dates with boys,

16:30.000 --> 16:32.000
I leave these two words.

16:32.000 --> 16:35.000
Watch out.

16:35.000 --> 16:40.000
Signed, sealed, and delivered, Chester A. Reilly.

16:40.000 --> 16:42.000
Those were my last words.

16:42.000 --> 16:43.000
Well, I hope so.

16:43.000 --> 16:45.000
Of all the nonsense I ever heard.

16:45.000 --> 16:46.000
Come on, now.

16:46.000 --> 16:47.000
Let's get started.

16:47.000 --> 16:49.000
All right, Peg.

16:49.000 --> 16:54.000
Babs, be a good girl and take care of Junior.

16:54.000 --> 16:58.000
Junior, be a good girl and take care of your sister.

16:58.000 --> 17:00.000
Oh, Pop, you're going to be OK.

17:00.000 --> 17:01.000
Oh, of course, Reilly.

17:01.000 --> 17:02.000
Are you coming?

17:02.000 --> 17:03.000
All right, Peg.

17:03.000 --> 17:08.000
But before I go, let me get one last look at my family.

17:08.000 --> 17:09.000
Don't move.

17:09.000 --> 17:11.000
Stay right where you are.

17:11.000 --> 17:15.000
Gee, seeing you like this brings a big lump into my throat.

17:15.000 --> 17:16.000
Those are your tonsils.

17:16.000 --> 17:17.000
Come on.

17:17.000 --> 17:18.000
Let's get them out.

17:18.000 --> 17:19.000
All right.

17:22.000 --> 17:24.000
Nice family, family.

17:24.000 --> 17:25.000
Lost water.

17:25.000 --> 17:26.000
Take my pulse.

17:26.000 --> 17:27.000
Take my pulse.

17:27.000 --> 17:29.000
I just took your pulse, Mr. Reilly.

17:29.000 --> 17:30.000
It's normal.

17:30.000 --> 17:31.000
Now stop worrying.

17:31.000 --> 17:32.000
You're perfectly normal.

17:32.000 --> 17:33.000
I am not normal.

17:33.000 --> 17:35.000
I know myself better than you do.

17:35.000 --> 17:37.000
Why did I ever come here?

17:37.000 --> 17:39.000
Why did I ever let that doctor look at my tonsils?

17:39.000 --> 17:41.000
I'll never open my big mouth again.

17:41.000 --> 17:42.000
Now try to relax.

17:42.000 --> 17:43.000
Look at the way you act.

17:43.000 --> 17:44.000
You think you were going to die.

17:44.000 --> 17:46.000
I like to look ahead.

17:46.000 --> 17:48.000
Where's my late widow?

17:48.000 --> 17:49.000
She should have been back by now.

17:49.000 --> 17:51.000
She went out for some lunch.

17:51.000 --> 17:54.000
She'll be here when you get back from the operating theater.

17:54.000 --> 17:55.000
See?

17:55.000 --> 17:56.000
Nothing doing.

17:56.000 --> 17:58.000
Nobody's selling tickets to look at me.

17:58.000 --> 18:00.000
They call the surgery room.

18:00.000 --> 18:02.000
Now I better get you ready.

18:02.000 --> 18:04.000
You mean my time has come?

18:04.000 --> 18:06.000
I'm going to give you something for your nerves.

18:06.000 --> 18:07.000
You'll feel better.

18:07.000 --> 18:10.000
You mean you're going to stab me with that dagger?

18:10.000 --> 18:13.000
Just a hypodermic needle, and it won't hurt a bit.

18:13.000 --> 18:15.000
Now just turn your head, and it'll be over before you know it.

18:15.000 --> 18:16.000
They murdered her.

18:16.000 --> 18:18.000
They murdered her.

18:18.000 --> 18:21.000
Now close your eyes.

18:21.000 --> 18:22.000
Ow!

18:22.000 --> 18:23.000
Ow!

18:23.000 --> 18:24.000
Ow!

18:24.000 --> 18:25.000
My arm!

18:25.000 --> 18:26.000
My arm!

18:26.000 --> 18:27.000
Get back in bed.

18:27.000 --> 18:29.000
All I did was swab your arm with alcohol.

18:33.000 --> 18:35.000
Now lie still.

18:39.000 --> 18:42.000
Well, why don't you do it and get it over with?

18:42.000 --> 18:43.000
It's all done, Mr. Riley.

18:43.000 --> 18:45.000
I told you it wouldn't hurt.

18:47.000 --> 18:49.000
I guess it was a dull needle.

18:49.000 --> 18:50.000
Now try to relax.

18:50.000 --> 18:53.000
The orderlies will come and get you with a stretcher in a few minutes.

18:53.000 --> 18:56.000
Where's my late widow and my children?

18:56.000 --> 18:57.000
They're waiting in the green room.

18:57.000 --> 18:59.000
Now try to go to sleep.

18:59.000 --> 19:00.000
Sleep?

19:00.000 --> 19:01.000
Not me.

19:01.000 --> 19:05.000
I'm staying awake to make sure that doctor knows what he's doing.

19:05.000 --> 19:07.000
I'm not taking any chances.

19:07.000 --> 19:09.000
Oh, nurse, please give this to the supervisor.

19:09.000 --> 19:10.000
Yes, Dr. Harvey.

19:10.000 --> 19:12.000
And are you ready for Mr. Riley?

19:12.000 --> 19:13.000
Riley?

19:13.000 --> 19:14.000
Yes, this case here.

19:14.000 --> 19:15.000
He's asleep.

19:15.000 --> 19:17.000
Oh, yes, the tonsillectomy.

19:17.000 --> 19:20.000
Well, I have a serious emergency that just came in.

19:20.000 --> 19:23.000
I won't be able to get to Mr. Riley until sometime this afternoon.

19:23.000 --> 19:24.000
You'd better take him back to his room.

19:24.000 --> 19:25.000
Yes, doctor.

19:29.000 --> 19:30.000
Hey, Mom.

19:30.000 --> 19:32.000
Mom.

19:32.000 --> 19:34.000
I just got a call from the hospital.

19:34.000 --> 19:37.000
Hey, Mom, Mom.

19:37.000 --> 19:39.000
I just saw him wheel Pop into his room.

19:39.000 --> 19:41.000
Then the operation must be over.

19:41.000 --> 19:42.000
He certainly was quick.

19:42.000 --> 19:44.000
Well, I hope Daddy's all right.

19:44.000 --> 19:45.000
Shh.

19:45.000 --> 19:46.000
Let's go in.

19:51.000 --> 19:52.000
Poor thing is jealously.

19:52.000 --> 19:53.000
It's the anesthetic.

19:53.000 --> 19:55.000
I guess it takes a dope to swallow her off.

19:55.000 --> 19:56.000
Where's the nurse?

19:56.000 --> 19:58.000
He shouldn't be left alone after an operation.

19:58.000 --> 20:00.000
All right, jealous, it's my time.

20:00.000 --> 20:01.000
I'm coming, too.

20:01.000 --> 20:03.000
Riley, dear, it's me, Peg.

20:03.000 --> 20:04.000
Where am I?

20:04.000 --> 20:05.000
You're back in your room.

20:05.000 --> 20:07.000
The operation's all over.

20:07.000 --> 20:09.000
It's all over?

20:09.000 --> 20:11.000
Yes, how do you feel?

20:11.000 --> 20:13.000
Oh, my throat.

20:13.000 --> 20:14.000
It must be the hurt from the shot.

20:14.000 --> 20:15.000
Oh, it's agony.

20:15.000 --> 20:17.000
But I can take it.

20:17.000 --> 20:18.000
Oh, the pain.

20:18.000 --> 20:20.000
We'd better call the doctor.

20:20.000 --> 20:21.000
No, don't call the doctor.

20:21.000 --> 20:24.000
I'd rather suffer in silence.

20:24.000 --> 20:26.000
Oh, the pain.

20:26.000 --> 20:27.000
Oh, dear.

20:27.000 --> 20:29.000
Take a sip of water.

20:29.000 --> 20:30.000
I can't swallow.

20:30.000 --> 20:31.000
Come on, Pop, try.

20:31.000 --> 20:32.000
Be brave.

20:32.000 --> 20:33.000
I'll help you.

20:33.000 --> 20:34.000
OK.

20:36.000 --> 20:37.000
Did it hurt?

20:37.000 --> 20:40.000
Oh, the pain.

20:40.000 --> 20:42.000
It's excruciating.

20:42.000 --> 20:43.000
Take another sip.

20:43.000 --> 20:44.000
Come on.

20:50.000 --> 20:52.000
Hey, that didn't hurt at all.

20:52.000 --> 20:54.000
Don't sound so hoarse, dear.

20:54.000 --> 20:56.000
Well, you sound more like yourself, Daddy.

20:56.000 --> 20:58.000
I feel fine.

20:58.000 --> 21:00.000
I tell you, Peg, that modern surgery is wonderful.

21:00.000 --> 21:02.000
Oh, I'm so glad you came through it all, Riley.

21:02.000 --> 21:04.000
And you will worry.

21:04.000 --> 21:05.000
Oh, it's wonderful.

21:05.000 --> 21:07.000
But I don't understand how.

21:07.000 --> 21:08.000
About the will.

21:08.000 --> 21:10.000
I was only kidding about that $15.

21:10.000 --> 21:12.000
There's no $15 behind the radio.

21:12.000 --> 21:13.000
There isn't now.

21:13.000 --> 21:16.000
It's right here in my bag.

21:16.000 --> 21:17.000
Hello, Riley.

21:17.000 --> 21:18.000
Oh, hiya, Doc.

21:18.000 --> 21:19.000
How are you feeling?

21:19.000 --> 21:20.000
I feel great.

21:20.000 --> 21:22.000
Doc, you certainly know your business all right.

21:22.000 --> 21:23.000
Thank you.

21:23.000 --> 21:24.000
I feel good enough to go home.

21:24.000 --> 21:26.000
Well, that's fine.

21:26.000 --> 21:27.000
I'll send the stretcher right in.

21:27.000 --> 21:29.000
Oh, I don't need no stretcher to get to the bus.

21:29.000 --> 21:32.000
Riley, you're certainly a card.

21:32.000 --> 21:33.000
Yeah.

21:33.000 --> 21:34.000
But don't worry.

21:34.000 --> 21:36.000
I'll have you out of that operating room in no time.

21:36.000 --> 21:38.000
Operating room?

21:38.000 --> 21:39.000
What operating room?

21:39.000 --> 21:41.000
I thought the operation was over.

21:41.000 --> 21:43.000
I certainly wish it were.

21:43.000 --> 21:46.000
I'm so tired, I can't see straight.

21:46.000 --> 21:49.000
Do you mean that I wasn't up?

21:49.000 --> 21:51.000
That I didn't just...

21:51.000 --> 21:53.000
That I still got them?

21:53.000 --> 21:54.000
Let me out!

21:54.000 --> 21:55.000
Let me out!

21:55.000 --> 21:56.000
Let me out!

21:56.000 --> 21:59.000
Let me out!

